{
  // Type-checking for `npm run check`, without the generated files.
  //
  // tsconfig.json deliberately includes `.next/types` and `.next/dev/types`
  // so editors and `next build` see Next's generated route types. Those
  // files are also rewritten continuously by a running dev server, and a
  // half-written one makes tsc fail with a parse error in a file nobody
  // wrote:
  //
  //   .next/dev/types/validator.ts(892,1): error TS1128
  //
  // That is not a defect in the codebase, it is a race with another
  // process — and it has already defeated one local build and one run of
  // this check. A pre-push check that fails for reasons the author cannot
  // act on is a check that stops being run, which is how the lint rules
  // went unenforced.
  //
  // So this profile checks the source and leaves the generated types to
  // `next build`, which generates them itself and is the authority on
  // whether they are right.
  //
  // `exclude` alone was NOT enough, and this is the subtle part.
  // next-env.d.ts ends with:
  //
  //   import "./.next/dev/types/routes.d.ts";
  //
  // and an import pulls a file in regardless of `exclude`, which only
  // filters the initial file list. So listing next-env.d.ts here quietly
  // re-admitted the very file this profile exists to keep out, and
  // `npm run check` still failed with a parse error in routes.d.ts
  // whenever a dev server happened to be writing it. Observed again on
  // 2026-11-14, with the file truncated mid-declaration on disk.
  //
  // next-env.d.ts contributes nothing else that matters: its other two
  // lines are `reference types` directives, which `types` below supplies
  // directly.
  //
  // It has to be named in `exclude`, not merely left out of `include`:
  // it is a .ts file in the project root, so `**/*.ts` matches it either
  // way. Dropping it from `include` alone changes nothing, which is how
  // the first attempt at this fix still failed.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "types": ["next", "next/image-types/global", "node"]
  },
  "include": [
    "**/*.ts",
    "**/*.tsx",
    "**/*.mts"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    ".next",
    "next-env.d.ts"
  ]
}
